INFO 08-27 10:21:43 logger.py:39] Received request chatcmpl-04785f43a9c341bd860289ba5182b390: prompt: '<|im_start|>system\nYou are an expert AI Curriculum Director.\n\n\n            As a genius expert, your task is to understand the content and provide\n            the parsed objects in json that match the following json_schema:\n\n\n            {\n  "description": "Schema for Agent 0: Curriculum Director / Problem Formulation Agent",\n  "properties": {\n    "title": {\n      "description": "Domain-grounded title of the coding exercise",\n      "title": "Title",\n      "type": "string"\n    },\n    "domain_context": {\n      "description": "Summary of Phase 1 dataset, task, and class labels derived dynamically from telemetry",\n      "title": "Domain Context",\n      "type": "string"\n    },\n    "problem_statement": {\n      "description": "Detailed exercise directive focusing on Phase 1 failure modes (e.g. high false negative/positive rates, low precision, segmentation or regression error)",\n      "title": "Problem Statement",\n      "type": "string"\n    },\n    "learning_objectives": {\n      "description": "2-3 specific learning outcomes based on Bloom\'s taxonomy",\n      "items": {\n        "type": "string"\n      },\n      "title": "Learning Objectives",\n      "type": "array"\n    },\n    "target_input_shape": {\n      "description": "Tensor shape contract for synthetic input (e.g. [batch_size, channels, ...] or [batch_size, seq_len, features])",\n      "title": "Target Input Shape",\n      "type": "string"\n    },\n    "target_output_shape": {\n      "description": "Tensor shape contract for model output (e.g. [batch_size, num_classes] or [batch_size, 1, H, W])",\n      "title": "Target Output Shape",\n      "type": "string"\n    },\n    "suggested_focus": {\n      "description": "Core technical implementation focus (e.g. Weighted Loss, Feature Attribution Hooks, Custom Layers, Data Augmentation)",\n      "title": "Suggested Focus",\n      "type": "string"\n    },\n    "markdown_overview": {\n      "description": "Comprehensive Markdown document (.md) explaining: (1) The core PyTorch/Deep Learning concept, (2) How it directly relates to the Phase 1 dataset telemetry & failure modes, and (3) What the student is trying to solve in the hands-on exercise.",\n      "title": "Markdown Overview",\n      "type": "string"\n    }\n  },\n  "required": [\n    "title",\n    "domain_context",\n    "problem_statement",\n    "learning_objectives",\n    "target_input_shape",\n    "target_output_shape",\n    "suggested_focus",\n    "markdown_overview"\n  ],\n  "title": "ProblemStatementSchema",\n  "type": "object"\n}\n\n            Make sure to return an instance of the JSON, not the schema itself\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nYou are an expert AI Curriculum Director and Applied Deep Learning Educator.\nFormulate a domain-grounded coding problem statement for module \'NumPy Basics & Data Structures\' (Week 1).\nDirectives: Explore dataset directory structure, NumPy array operations, and matrix normalization.\nDifficulty: Beginner\n\n--- PHASE 1 PIPELINE TELEMETRY ---\nDataset/Config: skin_cancer_testing_config.yaml\nTotal Rows Processed: 3297\nOverall Accuracy: 90.63% | AUC-ROC: 0.9709\nClass Balance: {\'benign\': 1800, \'malignant\': 1497}\nError Telemetry: {\'benign_predicted_as_malignant\': 145, \'malignant_predicted_as_benign\': 164}\nPer-Class Metrics: {\'benign\': {\'precision\': 0.9098, \'sensitivity_recall\': 0.9194, \'specificity\': 0.8904, \'false_negative_rate\': 0.0806, \'false_positive_rate\': 0.1096, \'f1_score\': 0.9146}, \'malignant\': {\'precision\': 0.9019, \'sensitivity_recall\': 0.8904, \'specificity\': 0.9194, \'false_negative_rate\': 0.1096, \'false_positive_rate\': 0.0806, \'f1_score\': 0.8961}}\nClass Labels: {\'0\': \'benign\', \'1\': \'malignant\'}\n5-Fold CV Mean Accuracy: 0.8811 | Mean F1: 0.88\nPipeline Artifact Columns: [\'image_path\', \'ground_truth\', \'predicted_class\', \'probabilities\', \'segmented_image\', \'mask\']\n\n--- STATISTICAL CONTRASTIVE SAMPLES (AGENT 0 REFERENCE) ---\n[TOP_SUCCESS SAMPLE]: {\'image_path\': \'/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1539.jpg\', \'ground_truth\': \'benign\', \'predicted_class\': \'benign\', \'probabilities\': \'[0.9997190833091736, 0.00028089064289815724]\', \'segmented_image\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/segmented/1539_segmented_20260827_100725.png\', \'mask\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/masks/1539_mask_20260827_100725.png\'}\n[HARD_FAILURE SAMPLE]: {\'image_path\': \'/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1649.jpg\', \'ground_truth\': \'benign\', \'predicted_class\': \'malignant\', \'probabilities\': \'[0.06722459942102432, 0.9327754378318787]\', \'segmented_image\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/segmented/1649_segmented_20260827_100724.png\', \'mask\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/masks/1649_mask_20260827_100724.png\'}\n[BOUNDARY_UNCERTAINTY SAMPLE]: {\'image_path\': \'/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1303.jpg\', \'ground_truth\': \'benign\', \'predicted_class\': \'benign\', \'probabilities\': \'[0.5000357031822205, 0.49996432662010193]\', \'segmented_image\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/segmented/1303_segmented_20260827_100725.png\', \'mask\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/masks/1303_mask_20260827_100725.png\'}\n[MINORITY_SAMPLE SAMPLE]: {\'image_path\': \'/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1135.jpg\', \'ground_truth\': \'benign\', \'predicted_class\': \'benign\', \'probabilities\': \'[0.8951337337493896, 0.10486628115177155]\', \'segmented_image\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/segmented/1135_segmented_20260827_100716.png\', \'mask\': \'./output/skin_cancer_v1/images/masks/1135_mask_20260827_100716.png\'}\n\nFORMULATION DIRECTIVES:\n1. Analyze Phase 1 telemetry (error counts, class imbalance, precision/recall per class, and contrastive samples).\n2. Formulate a realistic, domain-specific problem statement using the exact target class names and dataset metrics provided in telemetry.\n3. Specify clear synthetic tensor input/output shape contracts matching the dataset modality.\n4. Focus the exercise on addressing the primary model failure modes and performance gaps discovered in Phase 1.\n5. Write a comprehensive `markdown_overview` document formatted in Github-flavored Markdown containing:\n   - `# [Module Title] Concept Overview`\n   - `## 1. Theoretical Background` (explaining the deep learning concept)\n   - `## 2. Domain & Pipeline Telemetry Grounding` (explaining how this concept connects to the Phase 1 dataset & error cases)\n   - `## 3. Hands-on Student Exercise & Objectives` (explaining what the student is building, implementing, and solving)\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=1.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=8192, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=GuidedDecodingParams(json=None, regex=None, choice=None, grammar=None, json_object=True, backend=None, whitespace_pattern=None)), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
