cer Classification (Week 1)\n\n## Domain Context & Background\nThe Phase 1 pipeline processed a skin cancer dataset across 3,297 samples with a configuration file named `skin_cancer_testing_config.yaml`. The overall performance metrics include an accuracy of 90.63% and an AUC-ROC of 0.9709. The dataset has class balance with 1800 benign and 1497 malignant samples. There were notable classification errors with 145 benign samples predicted as malignant and 164 malignant samples predicted as benign, affecting precision and recall for both classes.\n\n## Real-World Problem Directive\nDespite high overall accuracy, the model shows a significant number of misclassifications, particularly false negatives and false positives involving benign and malignant skin cancer samples. The task is to explore and manipulate the dataset using NumPy to understand these errors better and prepare data structures for further analysis and model improvement. Specifically, students will practice loading and manipulating dataset metrics in NumPy arrays, normalize these metrics, and explore how data structures can be used to process and mitigate specific error cases.\n\n## Machine Learning Concepts & Tensor Contracts\n- Target Input Shape: `[batch_size, num_features]`\n- Target Output Shape: `[batch_size, num_classes]`\n- Core Focus: Data manipulation and normalization using NumPy\n- Learning Objectives: Understand and apply basic NumPy array operations and manipulations., Normalize dataset features using NumPy to prepare data for machine learning models., Interpret dataset telemetry and error cases using NumPy to guide model improvements.\n\n## Pipeline Execution Telemetry\n- **Dataset Classes:** benign, malignant\n\n## Case Studies & Error Analysis\n- **High-Confidence Match:** `/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1539.jpg` (Classified correctly as benign)\n- **Diagnostic Failure Mode:** `/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1649.jpg` (