 15}, "quote_mark_icon": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"icon_query": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["icon_query"]}, "quote_body_text": {"type": "string", "minLength": 80, "maxLength": 159}, "attribution_text": {"type": "string", "minLength": 9, "maxLength": 17}}, "required": ["headline_text", "quote_mark_icon", "quote_body_text", "attribution_text"]}}, "required": ["background_stage", "center_quote_content"]}\n\n### Slide Layout: 9\n- Name: title_table_description\n- Description: A centered presentation layout with subtle side accents, prominent heading, rounded comparison card, and explanatory note beneath.\n- Schema: {"$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema", "type": "object", "title": "title_table_description", "description": "A centered presentation layout with subtle side accents, prominent heading, rounded comparison card, and explanatory note beneath.", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"title_header": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"main_title": {"type": "string", "minLength": 9, "maxLength": 17}}, "required": ["main_title"]}, "comparison_table_card": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"comparison_matrix_table": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"columns": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "minItems": 4, "maxItems": 4}, "rows": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}, "minItems": 4, "maxItems": 4}, "minItems": 4, "maxItems": 4}}, "required": ["columns", "rows"]}}, "required": ["comparison_matrix_table"]}, "bottom_note": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"supporting_note": {"type": "string", "minLength": 105, "maxLength": 210}}, "required": ["supporting_note"]}}, "required": ["title_header", "comparison_table_card", "bottom_note"]}\n\n### Slide Layout: 10\n- Name: table_of_contents\n- Description: A clean contents slide with centered heading, small decorative accent, and balanced columns of navigation rows.\n- Schema: {"$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema", "type": "object", "title": "table_of_contents", "description": "A clean contents slide with centered heading, small decorative accent, and balanced columns of navigation rows.", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"centered_title_block": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"main_heading": {"type": "string", "minLength": 9, "maxLength": 30}}, "required": ["main_heading"]}, "table_of_content_items_grid": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"items_grid": {"type": "array", "minItems": 2, "maxItems": 10, "items": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"item_number": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 2}, "item_label": {"type": "string", "minLength": 4, "maxLength": 22}, "page_number": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 2}}, "required": ["item_number", "item_label", "page_number"]}}}, "required": ["items_grid"]}}, "required": ["centered_title_block", "table_of_content_items_grid"]}\n\n### Slide Layout: 11\n- Name: title_description_team_cards\n- Description: A clean split presentation layout with introductory copy on the left and a profile card grid on the right.\n- Schema: {"$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema", "type": "object", "title": "title_description_team_cards", "description": "A clean split presentation layout with introductory copy on the left and a profile card grid on the right.", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"left_intro_block": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"intro_vertical_stack": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"intro_heading": {"type": "string", "minLength": 8, "maxLength": 25}, "intro_body": {"type": "string", "minLength": 64, "maxLength": 250}}, "required": ["intro_heading", "intro_body"]}}, "required": ["intro_vertical_stack"]}, "profile_card_grid": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"profile_grid": {"type": "array", "minItems": 4, "maxItems": 4, "items": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"profile_photo": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"image_prompt": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["image_prompt"]}, "profile_name": {"type": "string", "minLength": 7, "maxLength": 20}, "profile_role": {"type": "string", "minLength": 2, "maxLength": 25}, "profile_description": {"type": "string", "minLength": 45, "maxLength": 100}}, "required": ["profile_photo", "profile_name", "profile_role", "profile_description"]}}}, "required": ["profile_grid"]}}, "required": ["left_intro_block", "profile_card_grid"]}\n\n\n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n## Slide 1:\n  - Content: content=\'# NumPy Basics & Data Structures for Skin Cancer Classification\\n- **Course Module:** DigitalAgEdu Applied Deep Learning Suite (Week 1)\\n- **Domain Application:** The Phase 1 pipeline processed a skin cancer dataset across 3,297 samples with a configuration file named `skin_cancer_testing_config.yaml`. The overall performance metrics include an accuracy of 90.63% and an AUC-ROC of 0.9709. The dataset has class balance with 1800 benign and 1497 malignant samples. There were notable classification errors with 145 benign samples predicted as malignant and 164 malignant samples predicted as benign, affecting precision and recall for both classes.\\n- **Difficulty Level:** Beginner\' \n## Slide 2:\n  - Content: content=\'# Real-World Domain Challenge: NumPy Basics & Data Structures for Skin Cancer Classification\\n- **Problem Directive:** Despite high overall accuracy, the model shows a significant number of misclassifications, particularly false negatives and false positives involving benign and malignant skin cancer samples. The task is to explore and manipulate the dataset using NumPy to understand these errors better and prepare data structures for further analysis and model improvement. Specifically, students will practice loading and manipulating dataset metrics in NumPy arrays, normalize these metrics, and explore how data structures can be used to process and mitigate specific error cases.\\n- **Dataset Classes:**\' \n## Slide 3:\n  - Content: content=\'# Machine Learning Principles & Architecture\\n- **Tensor Shape Contract:** Input `[batch_size, num_features]` → Output `[batch_size, num_classes]`\\n- **Core Technique:** Data manipulation and normalization using NumPy\\n- **Learning Outcomes:**\\n  * Understand and apply basic NumPy array operations and manipulations.\\n  * Normalize dataset features using NumPy to prepare data for machine learning models.\\n  * Interpret dataset telemetry and error cases using NumPy to guide model improvements.\' \n## Slide 4:\n  - Content: content="# PyTorch Reference Architecture\\n```python\\nimport torch\\nimport torch.nn as nn\\nfrom torchvision.models import vit_b_16, ViT_B_16_Weights\\n\\nclass CustomViT(nn.Module):\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        super(CustomViT, self).__init__()\\n        # Load the vit_b_16 model with ImageNet weights\\n        self.vit = vit_b_16(weights=ViT_B_16_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1)\\n        # Replace the final fully connected layer to output 10 classes\\n        num_ftrs = self.vit.heads.head.in_features\\n        self.vit.heads.head = nn.Linear(num_ftrs, 10)\\n\\n    def forward(self, x):\\n        # Forward pass through the network\\n        return self.vit(x)\\n\\n# Example usage (no need to modify)\\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\\n    model = CustomViT()\\n    x = torch.randn(4, 3, 224, 224)  # Batch of 4 images, each 224x224 pixels, 3 color channels\\n    output = model(x)\\n    print(output.shape)  # Should print" \n## Slide 5:\n  - Content: content=\'# Model Evaluation & Diagnostic Case Studies\\n- **Error Distribution & Real-World Impact:**\\n- **High-Confidence Match:** `/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1539.jpg` (Classified correctly as benign)\\n- **Diagnostic Failure Mode:** `/fs/ess/PAS2699/digitalAgEdu_datasets/skin_cancer_dataset/benign/1649.jpg` (True: benign, Predicted: malignant)\\n- **Mitigation Strategy:** Addressing false negatives and subtle decision boundary shifts\' \n<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n', params: SamplingParams(n=1, presence_penalty=0.0, frequency_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0, temperature=1.0, top_p=1.0, top_k=-1, min_p=0.0, seed=None, stop=[], stop_token_ids=[], bad_words=[], include_stop_str_in_output=False, ignore_eos=False, max_tokens=8192, min_tokens=0, logprobs=None, prompt_logprobs=None, skip_special_tokens=True, spaces_between_special_tokens=True, truncate_prompt_tokens=None, guided_decoding=GuidedDecodingParams(json={'properties': {'slides': {'description': 'List of slide layouts', 'items': {'type': 'integer'}, 'maxItems': 5, 'minItems': 5, 'title': 'Slides', 'type': 'array'}}, 'required': ['slides'], 'title': 'PresentationStructureModelWithNSlides', 'type': 'object'}, regex=None, choice=None, grammar=None, json_object=None, backend='xgrammar', whitespace_pattern=None)), prompt_token_ids: None, lora_request: None, prompt_adapter_request: None.
